'' A STRING CONST NAMED THROUGH A NAMESPACE -- 'ns.P', and a module's exported const, which
'' an importer names the same way -- passed to a 'byref as string' parameter of a USER
'' procedure. It was handed over as a POOL descriptor (fb_StrAllocTempDescZEx), and the
'' callee's first string call recycled it: 'for i = 1 to len( s )' over 'mid( s, i, 1 )' saw
'' an empty string. fbc copies it into a real temporary, as it does for a bare const --
'' and so it does for a property getter, 'o.Name', which came back empty the same way.
'' RUN, because the IR verifies either way.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/str-byref-qualified-const.bas -o tests/driver/strbyrefqconst.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/strbyrefqconst.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/strbyrefqconst.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: member plain 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: nested deep 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bare plain 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: using plain 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [PLAIN] [plain]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: property field 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: written field+
